module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unused_import_of_a_missing_module_is_accepted

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data unused_import_of_a_missing_module_is_accepted: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "unused_import_of_a_missing_module_is_accepted" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "**importing a nonexistent module and using nothing from it was accepted silently** (INVALID STATE: an `import` names a dependency; the native NamespaceOnlyY admission checked only captured alias rows, so a missing module whose listed names were unused — or whose block was empty and yielded zero rows — never reached module_root_find, and the program was Accepted. HARM: DESIGN section 5 silent wrongness — an unresolvable dependency is indistinguishable from a module that imports nothing).",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. Seed resolve_module_imports still walks every import node and refuses UnresolvedImport regardless of use (compile_fixture control unused_import_of_a_missing_module_refuses). Native acquisition already requests each import decl (v2.compiler.module_acquisition acquisition_read_requests). The drop is the native resolver: admit_captured_import_rows under NamespaceOnlyY, fed only AliasBindingRow values. Controls: unused missing refuses; unused real still accepts; used missing keeps its refusal.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: silent on the native NamespaceOnlyY admission path; mechanically preventable on the seed resolve_import path (blocking UnresolvedImport). RUNG NOW: mechanically preventable on both — native refuses with resolve_module_not_found at the authored import declaration (v2.compiler.name_resolve admit_imported_modules projects module_root_find's refusal onto CapturedImportTarget.at, the span-index extent of the import decl captured with the alias rows). CEILING: structurally guaranteed — every import decl's target is a carried QualifiedName with its authored locus, and admission has no Accepted arm that skips module_root_find. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: imported_modules is part of NormalizedTree construction so a hand-built tree cannot omit the import modules the parse named; until then a fixture that forgets the field can still Accept a missing import.",

    "CONSUMPTION: this per-class record joins the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster recurring_failure_mode_roster. Enrolled controls: v2.test.claim.name_resolve.admission_fail_closed unused_missing_import_refuses_under_namespace_only (reason and import-line locus) and unused_existing_import_accepts_under_namespace_only (native NamespaceOnlyY); v2.test.claim.unused_missing_import unused_import_of_a_missing_module_refuses (seed compile_fixture) and unused_missing_import_refusal_is_located_at_the_import_line (parse capture inhabitance of that locus).",
    "2026-10-17 (quick-dove-37, node adhoc-4466914d-f21): RECEIPT THAT THE RUNG IS CLOSURE-SCOPED, NOT CORPUS-WIDE — read RUNG NOW as 'no missing-module import survives a closure that is handed to the compiler', never as 'the corpus is scanned'. dag/test/claim/roadmap/roadmap_publication_push_real_execution.dag (added 2026-10-14 by 46010597b, #13844) shipped `import v2.std.live_tree { LiveTreeDisposition, SubstrateInputsOnly }`: no v2.std.live_tree exists in either governed root. THE SPELLING CENSUS IS `git grep -F -l <literal> <rev>` AT c4dc2576872 (counted over files, whole tree, no path filter): the bad spelling returns 1 file — this one — against 1794 for `import std.live_tree` and 1506 for the exact shape the witness means, `import std.live_tree { LiveTreeDisposition, SubstrateInputsOnly }` (its `data live_tree_disposition: LiveTreeDisposition = SubstrateInputsOnly` row names exactly those two symbols, both declared in dag/std/live_tree.dag, `module std.live_tree`). The refusal fired the moment the file WAS handed to the compiler — measured, not inferred: at origin/main 0b39d13a55d, `claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <that file> --functions <all four> --wet` refuses the whole file with `error: unresolved import: module 'v2.std.live_tree' not found`; after the one-line fix all four claims PASS at 1453ab30b1e — but NOTHING on any required path hands it to the compiler: three places name the file repo-wide (itself, its exclusion row, its wet schedule row) and none is a gate. WHY EACH GATE MISSES IT. (1) THE ADMISSION CLOSURE: gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots `witness_exclusion_frontier` carries a WitnessExclusionRow for it classified LocalRepoWetLane, so the required-floor prepared-subject closure excludes it and `admit_imported_modules` never sees it. (2) THE DECLARATION INDEX: it is a test witness module, the `OutsideDeclIndexTestWitnessModule` case std.decl_ref carries and v2.compiler.reference_conservation_admission documents, so `decl_facts` skips it. (3) THE WET LANE THAT WOULD HAVE RUN IT: its 4 claims are scheduled in v2.workflow.local_repo_wet_terminal `local_repo_wet_schedule` as WetScheduledClaim ExpectedToHold, but the Rust executor that consumed that schedule is gone — no `fn run_required_floor` exists on main, and the surviving mentions are comments recording it chain-deleted (f815c83d4e5, 'v1: chain-delete dead floor residue (B1/C)', 2026-10-15); the only live reader of `local_repo_wet_schedule_rows` is the required-lane-resolution census, which folds the rows into a module-identity population and never executes a claim, and no workflow invokes that instrument or passes `--wet` to claim_batch. So the 4 claims were dead twice over: unresolvable, and with no gate left that would ever have tried them. NOTE WHICH GATE WOULD HAVE CAUGHT IT, so the fix is aimed: the census DOES seed wet-schedule entries into the closure (required_floor_nominal_closure_module_seeds chains every row's entry_module), so the rung is sound where it is wired — this is a wiring gap, not a resolver gap. WHAT THIS ROW STILL DOES NOT COVER, and standing_gap stays open on exactly that: no gate admits every .dag under a governed root, so for a wet-lane witness, being read by the compiler at all is a favour from whoever thinks to invoke it.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.name_resolve", decl_name: "admit_imported_modules", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.normalize", decl_name: "import_binding_capture", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
